;; Phase A4 — symbol-pointer witness.
;;
;; Covers IR_LoadSymbolPointer for an arbitrary (non-#f / non-#t / non-_empty_)
;; symbol. The arm64 emit pattern is ADRP + ADD imm12, and the arm64-aware
;; ObjectGenerator fix-up writes imm21 (page diff) into the ADRP and imm12
;; (within-page offset) into the ADD so the materialised value is the
;; absolute address of the symbol slot in the synthetic table.
;;
;; The harness pins 'tag42 at synthetic-symtab offset 42 (0x2A) and pages
;; the symtab on a 256-byte boundary, so the low byte of the materialised
;; pointer is 42 regardless of segment layout. We then add 100 and return,
;; giving 142. Without the fix-up the imm21/imm12 stay zero, the pointer
;; points at the segment-base page, and the test would not return 142.

(defun fortytwo ()
  (+ 100 (logand (the-as int 'tag42) 255)))
